{"reference":"Judges 13","book":"Judges","chapter":13,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Wider Book","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter begins Samson’s story within the central sequence of deliverance narratives shaped by the pattern set out in Judges 2, though the individual episodes do not all follow every stage of that pattern in a fixed cycle. The announcement that Samson will “begin” to save Israel from the Philistines also signals that his story does not claim a completed deliverance.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_judges_013_e6a1e09bfc0c2ddb291e677f","reader_path_judges_013_4efadc93a753ef49cca48cf2"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}